* Linux swap
** What swap is
*** Backing store for anonymous pages
*** Swap-out and swap-in (major fault)
*** tmpfs and shared memory need it
*** mkswap, swapon, /proc/swaps
** Reclaim
*** Watermarks: min, low, high
*** kswapd and direct reclaim
*** Anonymous and file LRU lists
*** swappiness: relative I/O cost, 0 to 200
*** page-cluster readahead
** Swap areas
*** Partition or file
*** File: no holes, no copy-on-write
*** Btrfs: mkswapfile
*** Priorities and round-robin
left side
** Compressed swap
*** zram: compressed block device in RAM
*** zswap: compressed cache before disk swap
** Out of memory
*** Thrashing
*** PSI: some and full
*** Kernel OOM killer, oom_score_adj
*** systemd-oomd and earlyoom
*** cgroup memory.max, memory.swap.max
** Security
*** Encrypt the swap area
*** Swap file mode 0600, root
*** mlock() for secrets
*** Hibernation writes all RAM
** Configuration
*** Safe swap file procedure
*** Verify with swapon --show
*** Size by purpose
